1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,417
How can a teammate pick up an agent investigation without starting over? This is
Agent Context Across Platform, demonstrated with a local session handoff.

2
00:00:11,417 --> 00:00:23,917
An unfinished investigation has a goal, earlier attempts, open questions, and
access limits. A useful handoff should preserve all four, not just a confident
summary.

3
00:00:23,917 --> 00:00:34,625
The target is one reviewed share action for the sender and a simple starting point
for the recipient. Access, authentication, and human consent still matter.

4
00:00:34,625 --> 00:00:49,417
Capture the selected context, redact sensitive material, review the exact bundle,
and publish a snapshot. The receiving agent treats it as historical reference, not
permission to replay commands.

5
00:00:49,417 --> 00:01:02,875
The flow begins with a share request for the current investigation. This first
screen shows OneDrive intent, not a completed cloud upload. The demonstration then
uses local transport.

6
00:01:02,875 --> 00:01:16,292
The proposed cloud path asks for specific recipients. This is an audience-
selection prompt. It does not mean the local endpoint has authenticated a
recipient or granted cloud access.

7
00:01:16,292 --> 00:01:29,167
The review explicitly shows the local provider and omitted material. Secret
detection is only an aid. Publication waits for the human to approve the exact
contents and destination.

8
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:42,917
After approval, the agent reports a local JSON snapshot and link. This is a
reviewed summary, not the complete live runtime, and the localhost address works
only on this machine.

9
00:01:42,917 --> 00:01:56,125
The recipient supplies the local link and selects Copilot and a workspace.
Historical context can be imported, but source credentials, permissions, and tool
connections do not transfer.

10
00:01:56,125 --> 00:02:10,042
The recorded output reports restored context and a dataset match. It also
discloses an access denial: popularity statistics came from cached rankings. No
SQL was run.

11
00:02:10,042 --> 00:02:26,125
Next is secure, policy-aligned sharing through SharePoint and OneDrive. That
requires approved identity, scoped recipients, data controls, and live tenant
validation. Compliance is not established by this local demo.

12
00:02:26,125 --> 00:02:35,125
Contact our team to collaborate on the next phase: a simpler handoff that keeps
security, permissions, and evidence visible.
